    "body": "allocation_sourcing.py already ranks transfer and vendor candidates using cost, lead time and reliability. It can be extended to consider:\n\nRisk-adjusted delivery dates and the date stock is needed.\nAvailable vendor capacity, minimum order quantities and shipping modes.\nActual incremental cost—including freight and other agreed charges.\nTransfer availability without breaching the donor location’s own minimum stock.\nI would not automatically exclude overseas suppliers whenever risk exceeds 0.7. The score must first be tied to the relevant supplier or shipment; a local supplier may also be unavailable, late, or too expensive. Instead, compare feasible candidates and explain the trade-off.\n\nThe proposed store-to-store allocation is a larger extension: the current transfer logic selects a source that covers the deficit; it does not yet optimize allocation across multiple destination stores.",
